UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>The Doctor of Clinical Dentistry (Endodontics) will address increasing needs of the public sector for endodontic health care as well as a high demand from general dentists in public and private sector for this specialty training. </p> <p>It offers dentists the chance to consolidate and extend their skills in the specialisation of endodontics, notably, root canal treatment.</p> <h4>Structure</h4><p>The program will be directed by Associate Professor William Ha and presented by specialist clinicians and researchers. </p> <p>It will be based primarily at the Sydney Dental Hospital, with some sessions at the Westmead Centre for Oral Health. </p> <p>The program is primarily clinical based with blocks of seminars and preclinical sessions. </p> <p>You will also be required to complete a research project in the field of Endodontics or pulp biology, under the supervision of an academic staff member.</p>',
